      "updated_at": "2019-01-05T04:39:03Z",
      "body": "I never even created a GitHub remote in the first place, but I will eventually be handing over the project directory to people who are even more clueless than I am about workflowr and git - so I redefined wflow_git_remote() to avoid accidents via that route (although, obviously, that doesn't stop somebody using git to push directly to a remote).\r\n\r\nGiven that lots of research projects have confidentiality constraints I thought it might provide a degree of comfort for workflowr users if there was some project-level configuration that could be set to indicate the project is confidential and prevent pushing to a remote repo.\r\n\r\n(Maybe a [git pre-push hook](https://blog.ghost.org/prevent-master-push/ could be used to prevent git from pushing to a remote.)",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
